<!--
    loweredswitchheads (GH-468 finding 4): look for a lowered-switch cascade
    behind every head on the switch variable, not only the first in block order.

    `loweredswitch` recovers a cascade from a head: a compare on the most-compared
    variable that no other compare on it continues into. An unrelated test of that
    same variable is a head too, and upstream tried only the first. MSVC /O2
    inlines `and_chain(argc, argc*7)` and `cascade_switch(argc)` into `main`, so a
    `TEST EBX,EBX; JLE` (the inlined and_chain) is the first compare on argc and
    the 15-case binary-search tree over the same argc follows a loop mid-function;
    recovery from the TEST head finds no case, so the tree rendered as a goto
    ladder into a shared join.

    Bytes: `main` of ab_o2.exe from the issue testbed (MSVC 18 /O2, x86-64, 640
    bytes at 0x1400011e0), with the callees it names stubbed. argc is copied ECX
    into callee-saved EBX at entry; each case arm is `MOV EDX,c; JMP join` and the
    default is `MOV EDX,-1`, and the join prints EDX.

    Pass 1 (option loweredswitchheads off): only the TEST head is tried, recovers
    no case, and the tree renders as a goto ladder into the join.
    Pass 2 (default, on): the cascade behind the later head is re-rolled into a
    switch over argc with all fifteen cases and the default, each arm still
    assigning the value the join prints.

    The off pass runs first: the lowered-switch store is sticky across clear(), so
    a declined detection leaves no record behind.
-->
